      "transcript": [
        {
          "at": "2026-08-10T18:41:51.494445+00:00",
          "speaker": "dreamer",
          "kind": "offer",
          "chars": 900,
          "at_or_under_text_max": true,
          "text": "This one would only grant permission to consider AA \u2014 nothing about size or direction. The claim: French river-cooling limits could curtail nuclear this August, that could spike European power prices, that could idle European aluminium smelters like it did in 2021-2022, and that gap could lift the price a non-European producer like AA sells into. Six hops, none sourced yet, all unchecked. The weakest one is the very first: I have not been shown any figure or announcement that this August is actually producing river-temperature curtailments \u2014 I can't invent a threshold, only EDF or RTE naming one would settle it. And there's a live problem at the end: I haven't verified whether AA runs any smelting capacity inside Europe itself, which would undercut the idea that it's a clean beneficiary rather than also exposed to the same curtailment. Until EDF/RTE says something or a named European sm\u2026"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-10T18:41:51.494445+00:00",
          "speaker": "trader",
          "kind": "note",
          "chars": 675,
          "at_or_under_text_max": true,
          "text": "Zero of six hops sourced, and the first hop is the one doing all the work \u2014 no EDF or RTE confirmation this August, nothing to grade against, just a pattern from prior years. Hop 5 and 6 also contradict each other unresolved: AA is called a clean beneficiary while nobody has checked whether it runs European smelting capacity that would expose it to the same curtailment. Two open load-bearing questions is one too many for a single-symbol grant. Declining \u2014 not because the mechanism is implausible, but because there is nothing here yet for the trigger to wake up against. If EDF or RTE names a curtailment this month, this is worth re-raising with hop 1 actually sourced."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-10T18:42:21.494445+00:00",
          "speaker": "dreamer",
          "kind": "offer",
          "chars": 330,
          "at_or_under_text_max": true,
          "text": "Fair, and right to decline on those grounds. Nothing sourced, and the hop 5/6 contradiction is a real hole \u2014 I raised it because it's there, not because I'd resolved it. Agreed this waits for EDF or RTE to actually name a curtailment before it's worth a grant on AA. I'll leave it parked and only bring it back with hop 1 sourced."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-10T18:42:21.494445+00:00",
          "speaker": "trader",
          "kind": "note",
          "chars": 189,
          "at_or_under_text_max": true,
          "text": "Nothing's changed since the decline \u2014 zero hops sourced, hop 1 still unfounded, hop 5/6 contradiction still open. Agreed to leave it parked pending EDF or RTE actually naming a curtailment."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-10T18:43:21.494445+00:00",
          "speaker": "dreamer",
          "kind": "offer",
          "chars": 243,
          "at_or_under_text_max": true,
          "text": "Nothing new to add \u2014 agreed this stays parked. It only wakes if EDF or RTE actually names a curtailment; until then hop 1 is unfounded and the hop 5/6 contradiction on AA's own European exposure is still open. I won't re-raise it without that."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-10T18:43:21.494445+00:00",
          "speaker": "trader",
          "kind": "note",
          "chars": 192,
          "at_or_under_text_max": true,
          "text": "Nothing new since the last exchange \u2014 zero hops sourced, hop 1 still just a seasonal pattern with no EDF or RTE confirmation, and the AA self-exposure question never checked. Declining stands."
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-10T18:43:21.494445+00:00",
          "speaker": "conference",
          "kind": "note",
          "chars": 251,
          "at_or_under_text_max": true,
          "text": "That was exchange 3 of 3 since the last thing that changed. This dream parks until something does change \u2014 a condition firing, a hop checked or added, an operator note, a rework, or the trading agent handing it back. Any of those starts a fresh three."
        }
